'''Banner''' skills are a sub-class of skills that can be manually activated to consume all Valour and place down a banner that provides an [[aura]]. The effect and radius of the Banner aura scales with the amount of Valour consumed. Valour is typically gained from [[melee]] combat.

==Mechanics==
Activating a Banner skill will place down that Banner in your current position, granting an [[aura]] to allies around it. Moving out the Banner's radius or activating the skill again will remove the Banner. 

A player is not ''inherently'' limited to 1 Banner. While the use of multiple Banners is usually prevented by {{c|mod|While you have no placed Banner, you can gain Valour}}, this may be circumvented with {{c|mod|Having a placed Banner does not prevent you gaining Valour}} on e.g. {{il|Perfidy}} or [[Worthy Causes]]. 

Similar to {{il|Plague Bearer}}, Banners cannot be [[trigger]]ed except by {{il|Automation}}. Automation will place a Banner if at least 1 Valour is available, then end the placement once off cooldown. 

===Valour===
Valour is a counter displayed on the buff bar that increases under certain conditions while you have a Banner skill. Valour augments the power of banner skills when they are placed, and is shared between all skills that care about Valour.<ref>https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3532389/page/1#35</ref> Valour normally cannot be gained while a Banner is placed. Earned valour does not expire over time, and is only lost when placing a banner or changing zones.

By default, players gain 1 Valour on melee kill (no more than once every 0.5 seconds), or on melee [[hit]] against {{c|rare|Rare}} or {{c|unique|Unique}} enemies (no more than once every 0.5 seconds), up to a maximum of 50. This gain is scaled by increases and reductions to Valour gained, though it does not reduce the internal cooldown of gaining Valour per-hit/kill. Enemies [[block]]ing the player's hits does not prevent Valour gain.

==Skill gems==
===Active skill gems===
{{Drop enabled gem table
|tables=skill_gems
|join=skill._pageID=skill_gems._pageID
|where=items.class_id="Active Skill Gem" AND items.name LIKE "%Banner" 
}}

===Support skill gems===
{{Drop enabled gem table
|tables=skill_gems
|join=skill._pageID=skill_gems._pageID
|where=items.class_id="Support Skill Gem" AND items.name LIKE "%Banner%" 
}}

==Related unique items==
The following [[unique item]]s are related to Banner skills:

{{Drop enabled unique item table
|tables=item_stats
|join=items._pageID=item_stats._pageID
|where=item_stats.id LIKE "%Banner%"
|large=1
|base_item=1
|level=1
|stat=1
}}

==Related passive skills==
===Passive skills===
The following [[passive skill]]s are related to Banners:
{{Query base passive skills
|where=passive_skill_stats.id LIKE "%Banner%" OR passive_skill_stats.id LIKE "%Valour%"
}}

===Cluster Jewel passive skills===
The following [[Cluster Jewel]] passives are related to banners:
{{Passive skill table
|q_where=passive_skills.id LIKE "affliction%"
     AND passive_skills.stat_text LIKE "%banner%"
|large=1
|stat_text=1
}}

===Ascendancy passive skills===
The following [[Ascendancy passive skill]]s are related to Banners:
{{Query ascendancy passive skills
|where=passive_skill_stats.id LIKE "%Banner%"
}}

===Masteries===
The following [[Passive Mastery|Masteries]] are related to Banners:
{{Query masteries|where=mastery_effects.stat_text_raw LIKE "%banner%" OR mastery_effects.stat_text_raw LIKE "%valour%"}}

===Tattoos/Runegrafts===
{{Drop enabled item table
|tables = tattoos
|join = items._pageID = tattoos._pageID
|where = items.class_id="StackableCurrency"
  AND tattoos.target IS NOT NULL
  AND items.description LIKE "%banner%"
|large=1
|description=1
}}

==Version history==
{{Version history table header}}
{{Version history table row|3.25.0|
* Banners have been reworked. Instead of having a [[reservation]] cost, they are now free. However they don't grant a permanent buff. Banners now need to be placed for the effect to be active, however once placed they are far more powerful than before. They also automatically deactivate once you leave their area. Additionally, there are new ways to prolong the effects, and more ways to invest in them than ever before.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.15.0|
* Defiance Banner has been added to the game.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.5.0|
